# Code Comment Rules

## Purpose

- Clarify design intent
- Make future changes and refactoring easier
- Improve readability and maintainability

---

## Comment Language

- Write comments in Japanese

---

## JSDoc Usage (Public Interface Only)

Use JSDoc for:

- Exported functions
- React components (default or named export)
- API route handlers (GET / POST / PUT / DELETE, etc.)
- Shared utilities used outside the file

Rules:

- Keep within 1–6 lines
- Describe behavior, responsibility, and constraints
- Do not describe implementation details
- Do not use @param or @returns

Example:

/\*\*

- 地図ページ
- - スポットを取得してピン表示する
- - フィルタ条件でクライアント側絞り込みを行う
    \*/

---

## `//` Comments (Internal Logic Only)

Use `//` only for:

- Helper functions inside components
- Important logic inside useEffect / useMemo
- Non-obvious design decisions
- Security, performance, or trade-off explanations

Rules:

- Keep to 1–2 lines
- Focus on "why", not "what"
- Do not write line-by-line explanations
- Do not restate obvious code behavior

Examples:

// APIの成功判定はHTTPだけでなくアプリ側ステータスも確認する
// レスポンス肥大化防止のためselectで取得項目を限定

---

## Commented-Out Code Policy

- Allowed only if the intent is explicitly documented
- Must include TODO if scheduled for removal
- Commented-out code without explanation is prohibited

Allowed:

// TODO: ageカラム削除後に削除予定
// age: body.age ?? null,

Prohibited:

// age: body.age ?? null,

---

## Prohibited

- Line-by-line explanatory comments
- Comments that restate the code
- Temporary debug comments left in the code
- Excessively long comments

---

## Cursor Instructions

- Add JSDoc to exported functions
- Use `//` only for non-obvious internal intent
- Suggest removing redundant comments
- Suggest removing unexplained commented-out code
